<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.10.5: Solving Inequalities</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00550</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.10.5: Solving Inequalities</md:title>
    <md:uuid>224a3a9e-5323-4cb7-b027-247dd4e7c40c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>In this activity, we’re going to solve inequalities. Work with a partner to solve each inequality given. Then match it with the number line representing its solution.</para>
      <para>As you complete the activity, discuss with your partner how you know each number line is the solution to its inequality.</para>
      <para>When you think you’ve found the correct number line for an inequality, substitute a test point that is on the highlighted part of the number line into the inequality. Is it true?</para>
      <para>Try a test point that is not highlighted. Is the inequality false? 
</para>
      <table class="os-raise-textheavytable">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis/>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis/>
            </entry>
          </row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(x\;–\;4\;\leq\;–6\;\)  </item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>Graph A <figure><media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 2. The number line to the right of 2 is highlighted."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_12_10_01.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(x\;+\;6\;\geq\;8\;\)</item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>Graph B <figure><media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on –2. The number line to the right of –2 is highlighted."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_12_10_02.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(4x\;\leq\;8\)  </item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>Graph C <figure><media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 2. The number line to the left of 2 is highlighted."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_12_10_03.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(–\frac12x\;\leq\;1\;\)</item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>Graph D <figure><media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on –2. The number line to the left of –2 is highlighted."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_12_10_04.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <para>Use the table to choose the matching graph to the inequality.</para>
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="c843f62e-01c0-467d-9b88-fd6d86e6fcd9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x\;–\;4\;\leq\;–6\;\)   </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph C.</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Graph C.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="aa58e8e3-0379-4543-add5-0a10093aa1ca" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x\;+\;6\;\geq\;8\;\) </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph A.</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Graph A.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="a7933e27-5d23-462c-812c-cf21352cb324" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(4x\;\leq\;8\)  </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph D.</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Graph D.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="d7ee986c-a3ab-4a2c-97f2-2781633811cd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(–\frac12x\;\leq\;1\;\) </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph B.</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Graph B.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <para>For each of the inequalities above, match it to the property you used to solve.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-textheavytable">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis/>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis/>
            </entry>
          </row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(x\;–\;4\;\leq\;–6\;\)  </item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>A. Multiplication Property of Inequality</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(x\;+\;6\;\geq\;8\;\)</item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>B. Addition Property of Inequality</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(4x\;\leq\;8\)  </item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>C. Division Property of Inequality</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                <item>\(–\frac12x\;\leq\;1\;\)</item>
              </list>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>C. Subtraction Property of Inequality</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="d0c3c61c-019a-41b3-8933-0a1c39a0c500" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x\;–\;4\;\leq\;–6\;\)   </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Addition Property of Inequality.</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Addition Property of Inequality.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="c5fbed53-4da9-41c4-88ce-cd9b6aa3659c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x\;+\;6\;\geq\;8\;\) </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Subtraction Property of Inequality.</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Subtraction Property of Inequality.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!--
        <p role="presentation">C or A</p>
     
        <p role="presentation">A or C</p>
 -->
      <!--BEGIN ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_30e5ad0a-53bd-4e8c-8f59-ed1cdc37135d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(4x\;\leq\;8\)   
          <para>Select <emphasis>two </emphasis>properties that could be used to solve the inequality</para>
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division Property of Inequality </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division Property of Inequality.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->
      <!--BEGIN ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_9aca208b-a54e-4a20-b884-3a200c574adc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(–\frac12x\;\leq\;1\;\) </para>
            <para>Select <emphasis>two </emphasis>properties that could be used to solve the inequality</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division Property of Inequality </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Multiplication Property of Inequality and Division Property of Inequality.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY MULTISELECTION 1 TRY -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Is there anything unique about the method used to solve \(–\frac12x\leq1\)? Explain.</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <span>Yes. The inequality contains a less than or equal to symbol \((\leq)\). However, in the solution there is a greater than or equal to symbol \((\geq)\). When using the Multiplication and Division Properties of Inequality, you must reverse the symbol when you multiply or divide by a negative number.</span>
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
